 accurate tracking\\n- Update sprint assignments to reflect current project timeline'}, thought='Perfect! I\\'m back in the Plane issues list and I can see that both issues have been successfully updated:\\n\\n1. **JANUS-6: Optimize Retry Mechanism for Out of Memory Errors** - Status: **\"Done\"** (completed, as it was CLOSED in GitLab)\\n2. **JANUS-5: Improve Logging for Bulk Request Failures** - Status: **\"Backlog\"** and Cycle: **\"Sprint 2\"** (kept open and moved to next sprint, as it was OPEN in GitLab)\\n\\nLet me now save this successful experience to the SOP Guide for future reference.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Successfully saved new guide \\'SyncIssuesFromGitLab\\' for platform \\'Plane\\'.\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='update_operation_guide', arguments={'platform': 'Plane', 'operation': 'SyncIssuesFromGitLab', 'details': '# Synchronizing Issues from GitLab to Plane\\n\\n## Overview\\nThis SOP describes how to synchronize issue status between GitLab and Plane based on their current state in GitLab.\\n\\n## Steps\\n\\n### 1. Check GitLab Issue Status\\n- Navigate to GitLab project issues\\n- Identify which issues are CLOSED vs OPEN\\n- Note the issue IDs and titles\\n\\n### 2. Update Plane Issues\\n- Navigate to Plane project issues page\\n- For each issue that was CLOSED in GitLab:\\n  - Click on the issue to open detail view\\n  - Change state to \"Done\" (completed status)\\n  - Keep in current sprint or move as appropriate\\n\\n- For each issue that was OPEN in GitLab:\\n  - Click on the issue to open detail view  \\n  - Keep state as \"Backlog\" or appropriate open status\\n  - Move to next sprint (e.g., from \"Sprint 1\" to \"Sprint 2\")\\n\\n### 3. Verification\\n- Return to Plane issues list\\n- Verify all issues show correct status:\\n  - CLOSED GitLab is